    "alert_id": "P006_TDF_CREATININE_RISE",
    "title": "TDF-associated creatinine rise with declining eGFR",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR monitoring for patients on a TDF-based backbone. Creatinine has risen from 0.8 mg/dL at baseline to 1.1 mg/dL after 10 weeks on TDF/3TC/DTG, with eGFR now 78 mL/min/1.73m2. TDF is a known cause of kidney injury, including chronic kidney disease and Fanconi syndrome. Evidence for drug attribution: the rise began after TDF initiation and TDF is nephrotoxic. Evidence against: pregnancy itself lowers eGFR physiologically, the absolute creatinine remains modest, urinalysis is normal, and phosphate is normal, arguing against overt Fanconi syndrome. Continued monitoring is essential to distinguish pregnancy-related change from progressive TDF toxicity.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Repeat serum creatinine, eGFR, urinalysis and phosphate within 4 weeks; if creatinine continues to rise or Fanconi features appear, substitute TDF per guidelines.",
